From: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 16:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] media: sunxi-cir: compute pulse durations from the sample rate

The driver converts each FIFO sample count to microseconds by multiplying
it by rx_resolution, an integer number of microseconds computed as
USEC_PER_SEC / (base_clk / 64). That is exact at the 8 MHz default (8 us)
but not at the 24 MHz the H713 DT asks for: the sample period is 2.667 us
and the integer division makes it 2, so every pulse and space is reported
0.75x its real length.

Measured with the stock remote on the H713 bench board: an NEC leader of
9000/4500 us arrived as 6716/3354 us and the data bits as 434/410 and
434/1250 us instead of 560/560 and 560/1690. The NEC decoder rejects all
of it, so no scancode was ever produced, while the raw lirc stream was
plainly NEC. Scaled by 4/3 offline, all 13 frames of the capture decode
with valid address and command checksums (address 0x00, POWER = 0x14,
matching stock's ir_power_key_code0).

Compute the duration from the clock rate instead, rounding to the nearest
microsecond, and round rx_resolution too since it is still reported to
userspace.

Signed-off-by: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/media/rc/sunxi-cir.c
+++ b/drivers/media/rc/sunxi-cir.c
@@ -98,6 +98,7 @@
 	struct reset_control *rst;
 	const char      *map_name;
 	bool		is_h713_vendor_init;
+	unsigned long	sample_hz;	/* base clock / 64 */
 };
 
 static irqreturn_t sunxi_ir_irq(int irqno, void *dev_id)
@@ -123,8 +124,9 @@
 			/* for each bit in fifo */
 			dt = readb(ir->base + SUNXI_IR_RXFIFO_REG);
 			rawir.pulse = (dt & 0x80) != 0;
-			rawir.duration = ((dt & 0x7f) + 1) *
-					 ir->rc->rx_resolution;
+			rawir.duration = DIV_ROUND_CLOSEST_ULL(
+				(u64)((dt & 0x7f) + 1) * USEC_PER_SEC,
+				ir->sample_hz);
 			ir_raw_event_store_with_filter(ir->rc, &rawir);
 		}
 	}
@@ -358,8 +360,14 @@
 	ir->rc->map_name = ir->map_name ?: RC_MAP_EMPTY;
 	ir->rc->dev.parent = dev;
 	ir->rc->allowed_protocols = RC_PROTO_BIT_ALL_IR_DECODER;
-	/* Frequency after IR internal divider with sample period in us */
-	ir->rc->rx_resolution = (USEC_PER_SEC / (b_clk_freq / 64));
+	/*
+	 * Frequency after IR internal divider. The sample period is not a
+	 * whole number of microseconds at every base clock (24 MHz gives
+	 * 2.667 us), so durations are computed from the rate rather than
+	 * from rx_resolution, which is only reported.
+	 */
+	ir->sample_hz = (clk_get_rate(ir->clk) ?: b_clk_freq) / 64;
+	ir->rc->rx_resolution = DIV_ROUND_CLOSEST(USEC_PER_SEC, ir->sample_hz);
 	ir->rc->timeout = IR_DEFAULT_TIMEOUT;
 	ir->rc->min_timeout = sunxi_ithr_to_usec(b_clk_freq, 0);
 	ir->rc->max_timeout = sunxi_ithr_to_usec(b_clk_freq, 255);
